-#
  CRW-11: what became of the SOS this car raised — sent, seen by a
  dispatcher, or the cars that are sent (BR-22). It follows the call on the
  open screen without sound: it is no live region, and no notice goes to
  the phones of the crew that asked.
- cars = [ sos.patrol_car, *sos.backups.reject(&:released_at).map(&:patrol_car) ].compact
- seen = sos.acknowledged_at
%section.crew-sos-state{ class: ("coming" if cars.any?) || ("seen" if seen),
  aria: { labelledby: "crew-sos-state-title" } }
  %h2#crew-sos-state-title
    - if cars.any?
      #{cars.map(&:call_sign).to_sentence} #{cars.one? ? 'is' : 'are'} sent to you
    - elsif seen
      The dispatcher has seen your SOS
    - else
      SOS sent at #{l(sos.received_at, format: '%H:%M')}
  %p
    - if cars.any?
      Dispatched at #{l(sos.dispatched_at, format: '%H:%M')}
      - if sos.accepted_at
        · accepted at #{l(sos.accepted_at, format: '%H:%M')}
      - if sos.arrived_at
        · arrived at #{l(sos.arrived_at, format: '%H:%M')}
    - elsif seen
      Sent at #{l(sos.received_at, format: '%H:%M')} · acknowledged at #{l(seen, format: '%H:%M')}
    - else
      The dispatcher has not acknowledged it yet.
